  "prefLabel": "Fis 402.06 Release of Fish",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Fis 402.06 Release of Fish.\n\n(a) No live fish shall be released in any waters of the state unless they shall be returned into the waters from where taken, except as permitted by the executive director under a permit to release specified in Fis 805.\n\n(b) No person shall possess any species of live fish except:\n\n(1) As permitted in Fis 402.08;\n\n(2) If the person is participating in a permitted bass tournament or intra-scholastic fishing tournament; or\n\n(3) If the person holds a current aquaculture permit, importation permit, possession permit, or permit to release for the fish in possession.\n\nSource. (See Revision Note #1 at chapter heading for Fis 400 and Revision Note at chapter heading for Fis 500) #5016, eff 1-1-91; EXPIRED 1-1-97\n\nNew. #6432, eff 1-21-97; ss by #6629, eff 1-1-98; ss by #8119, eff 1-1-05; ss by #9773-A, eff 1-1-11; ss by #10854, eff 6-22-15; ss by #14173, eff 1-9-25, EXPIRES: 1-9-35",
